message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of an “interactive card” that rotates (spins) when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** – no JavaScript required.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    margin:0;
}

/* ---------- Card container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 800px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D transform */
}
.card {
    width:260px;
    height:360px;
    position:relative;
    cursor:pointer;
    transition:transform .6s ease-in-out;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
}

/* ---------- Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* Rotate around Y‑axis */
}

/* ---------- Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-face {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* Hide backside while rotated */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.card-front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* Flip so it's visible after rotation */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- Sample content styling ---------- */
h2 {margin:0 0 10px;}
p {font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}
```

