<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front face -->
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/260/200?random=1" alt="Front image" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:8px;">
            <h2>Front Title</h2>
            <p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back face -->
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            <h2>Back Title</h2>
            <p>This side appears after the card flips. Add more details or actions here.</p>
            <button style="padding:.5rem 1rem;background:#007bff;color:white;border:none;border-radius:4px;">Action</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets `perspective` so the 3D rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both faces; `transform-style: preserve-3d` allows child elements to maintain 3D positioning. |
| `.card:hover` | Applies a 180° rotation around the Y‑axis when hovered. |
| `.card-face` | Common styles for front/back faces. |
| `.card-front` / `.card-back` | Each face has its own content. The back face is pre‑rotated 180° so it becomes visible after the card’s flip. |

Feel free to replace the placeholder images, text, or add more styling. If you want a different axis (e.g., X‑axis), change `rotateY` to `rotateX`. Enjoy your rotating card!
